00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:50,930
Zealander, Chinese, and Dutch.

48
00:03:51,890 --> 00:03:53,230
Finally, when.

49
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:54,950
About time.

50
00:03:55,430 --> 00:03:59,190
Neither the charts nor the question provides any specific period.

51
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:03,090
Therefore, let's use the present tense in this sample.

52
00:04:04,050 --> 00:04:07,590
Moving on to the great three, this is what we can find.

53
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:10,630
First, the subjects of comparison.

54
00:04:11,610 --> 00:04:16,410
Both the pie charts and the table list the same five specific nationalities.

55
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:18,430
So these are our subjects.

56
00:04:19,589 --> 00:04:21,510
Next, the global features.

57
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:26,330
Because there are no trends in these charts, let's focus on finding

