00:04:26,330 --> 00:04:27,850
two main comparisons.

59
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:33,750
Since we have two charts, we will choose one global feature for each.

60
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:38,250
Global feature number one comes from the pie chart.

61
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:43,090
Native Australians are the highest, or the most populous group.

62
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:47,130
Global feature number two comes from the table.

63
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:51,970
The Chinese population represents the highest urban population.

64
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:57,810
Now, let's practice writing this paragraph using the analysis we just did.

65
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:00,370
Look at the text on the screen.

66
00:05:01,190 --> 00:05:05,830
I have paraphrased the topic and summarized the global features, but key

67
00:05:05,830 --> 00:05:07,170
vocabulary is missing.

68
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:12,030
Use the information from the big three to fill blanks one and

69
00:05:12,030 --> 00:05:19,030
two, and use the great three, global features, to fill blanks three, four, and five.

