00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:23,550
You should give yourself one to two minutes to complete this task.

71
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:29,660
Let's go.

72
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:32,060
Let's check the possibilities.

73
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:39,160
For the first blank, if you wrote different nationalities, that is perfect and simple.

74
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:45,440
If you wrote various demographics, that is excellent academic vocabulary.

75
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:52,120
For the second blank, where they live is grammatically correct and very natural.

76
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:57,360
Location of residence is also a great noun phrase to use here.

77
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,880
Now, for the overview.

78
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:06,600
For blank three, looking at our global features, Australians, or native

79
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:09,480
Australians, are clearly the largest group.

80
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:14,960
By doing so, we are also able to fill in the blank four with Dutch.

81
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:21,160
For blank five, the Chinese population has the highest rate of city

82
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,540
living, so that fits perfectly.

83
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:28,800
And here it is, a complete sample at band six plus.

84
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:33,900
The pie chart illustrates the percentage of different nationalities in

85
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:38,140
Australia, while the table compares their location of residence.

86
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:43,420
It is clear from the pie chart that Australians represent the largest

87
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:47,180
